fter listening and agre…”"},{"id":"captain-tilney","name":"Captain Tilney","role":"minor","group":"g-tilney","firstAppearance":"s17","summary":"First mention: “Having heard the day before in Milsom Street that their elder brother, Captain Tilney, was expected almost every hour, she was at no loss for the name of a very fashionable-looking, handsome young man, whom she had ne…”"},{"id":"john","name":"John","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s5","summary":"First mention: “Allen, in a family of children; and when she expatiated on the talents of her sons, and the beauty of her daughters, when she related their different situations and views—that John was at Oxford, Edward at Merchant Ta…”"},{"id":"mr-morland","name":"Mr. Morland","role":"minor","group":"g-morland","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “Do go and see for her, Mr.”"},{"id":"general-tilney","name":"General Tilney","role":"minor","group":"g-tilney","firstAppearance":"s11","summary":"First mention: “It is General Tilney, my father.””"},{"id":"john-thorpe","name":"John Thorpe","role":"minor","group":"g-thorpe","firstAppearance":"s8","summary":"First mention: “John Thorpe, who in the meantime had been giving orders about the horses, soon joined them, and from him she directly received the amends which were her due; for while he slightly and carelessly touched the hand of Is…”"},{"id":"mrs-hughes","name":"Mrs. Hughes","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s9","summary":"First mention: “Allen, that she would move a little to accommodate Mrs.”"},{"id":"henry-tilney","name":"Henry Tilney","role":"minor","group":"g-tilney","firstAppearance":"s13","summary":"First mention: “Every other look upon an average was directed towards the opposite box; and, for the space of two entire scenes, did she thus watch Henry Tilney, without being once able to catch his eye.”"},{"id":"frederick","name":"Frederick","role":"minor","firstAppearance":"s20","summary":"First mention: ““I understand: she is in love with James, and f